    when: a reader selects a module
    then: the main area shows that module working: translations as a table, a type's fields, Create for each
          object the plugin can create, each surface rendered with the sample object, each operation run from a
          form built from its input schema with its result, a skill with the operations it gives the assistant
          (no model called), and the branches of App Graph that lead to the plugin's nodes, with those nodes
          marked

  req F-19.6:
    when: the reader creates or picks an object
    then: it is the sample object every module shows, chosen in the header

  req F-19.7:
    when: a learning-path page embeds the inspector
    then: the embed loads nothing until the reader clicks Load dev plugin, which fetches
          `http://localhost:3967/manifest.json` with the loader Composer uses; Reload loads it again after an
          edit, and a failed load says whether the server was unreachable, the manifest was invalid, or a module
          failed

  req F-19.8:
    when: a page embeds the inspector with the modules that page adds
    then: a "This page adds" box checks each against the loaded plugin, so the reader sees what is still missing

  req F-19.9:
    when: the docs site is built
    then: the inspector page carries an import map of the shared `@dxos/*` packages, as Composer does, so the
          reader's plugin uses the page's copies; the reader's package pins `@dxos/*` to the version the docs
          were built from

  req F-19.5:
    when: the inspector is published
    then: it is the package `@dxos/plugin-inspector`
```

```mdl
feat F-20: The tutorial plugin

  desc: |
    The PLEX learning path builds one plugin, Stash, as ECHO's builds one app ([F-15]). Each page writes one
    capability file and one region of `dx.config.ts`, and ends with the plugin as it stands, live in the inspector.

  req F-20.1:
    when: a PLEX learning-path page shows code
    then: the code is a region of the module the inspector embed loads, one capability module per page

  req F-20.2:
    when: a reader finishes a learning-path page that builds part of the plugin
    then: the page embeds the inspector, the reader loads their own plugin into it from its dev server, and no
          page before Run it in Composer needs Composer; The PLEX plugin alone loads the finished Stash
          plugin by itself
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: A sample that stops compiling fails the build.
  given: a snippet that calls `Obj.make`
  when: the signature of `Obj.make` changes incompatibly
  then: the site's build and typecheck fail, and the typecheck names the snippet
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: A planned page is visible, and marked.
  given: a `page` block with status `planned`
  when: the site is built
  then: the sidebar shows the page with a planned badge, and its route renders the stub template
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Both themes meet the contrast floor.
  given: the brand palette and syntax themes
  when: the theme script runs
  then: body text on the ground is at least 7:1, muted text and code tokens are at least 4.5:1, and
        the script fails otherwise
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: A phone can read the site.
  given: a 375 pixel wide viewport
  when: any spike page renders
  then: the page does not scroll sideways, and every line of a code sample is visible without scrolling
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: An agent gets the code, not the include.
  given: a page that includes a snippet
  when: an agent fetches the page's `.md` route
  then: the body contains the snippet's code and no `<Snippet` tag
```

