```mdl
decision D-200: HALO's app passes each device's services through React context: `openHalo` returns the services `@dxos/halo-adapter-client` makes from the client, the app and each embed device wrap the contact book in `HaloProvider` from `@dxos/halo-react`, and a component reads them with `useHaloServices()` and runs a piece with `.pipe(Effect.provide(services), Effect.runPromise)`. The `halo` and `run` props go away, and so does the app's own `useStream`: state comes from the package's hooks (`useIdentity`, `useSpaces`, `useMembers`, `useContacts`, `useDevices`, `useCredentials`, `useInvitationFlow`), and each step names the stream its hook follows. Changes stay Effects. `@dxos/halo-react` gains `useContacts`, which merges the members of every ready space by DID, leaves out the local identity and lists the spaces each contact shares; Contacts lists one row per contact on it.
