```mdl
decision D-208: Bookmarks saves links. A bookmark has `title`, `url` and `note`; `visits` and Record visit go away. The operation is Save link: it takes `{ url, title?, note? }`, adds a bookmark to the current space through `Database.Service`, files it with `DefaultParent.add`, and returns its URI, the way Composer's markdown Create operation does. Its App Graph action sits on the space's Bookmarks section and saves the address on the clipboard. The article edits the title and note and no longer runs an operation. The skill tells the assistant to save a link the user wants to keep, with a short title and their note. The inspector's operation form shows an input for an optional text field and leaves an empty field out of the input.
  date: 2026-11-12
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [plex-the-plex-plugin, app-framework-define-type, app-framework-add-operation, app-framework-extend-app-graph, app-framework-add-surface, plex-run-in-composer, app-framework-operations, plex-guide-testing, app-framework-publishing]
  why: A bookmark whose only operation counted visits was a counter, not something a person would use. Saving a link with a note is what a bookmark is for, and it gives the assistant a natural reason to run the operation.
```

```mdl
decision D-209: The four live demos also appear on the PLEX Overview, under What you can build. Each demo, there and on `/echo`, has a narrative beside it. On `/echo` the narrative is about the data: the objects in the space and what ECHO does as peers edit, go offline and reconnect. On the PLEX Overview it is about the plugins: which plugins render the demo, what each contributes, and how they meet over the same objects. Both narratives sit in one file beside the demos, so the two pages describe the same demos. On the PLEX Overview each demo runs in its own iframe, with its own two peers and space, like the other embeds on docs pages.
  date: 2026-11-12
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [app-framework-welcome, F-7.9, F-7.10]
  why: The demos show what you can build with PLEX as well as what ECHO does, and a reader needs to be told what they are looking at.
  rejected:
    - The `/echo` React islands placed directly on the Overview: docs pages keep app CSS in iframes, so the islands' theme styles would reach the Starlight page.
```

```mdl
decision D-210: The Bookmarks operation is Mark as read, which makes Bookmarks a reading list. A bookmark has `title`, `url`, `note` and `read`. Mark as read takes `{ bookmark }`, a reference to a bookmark, resolves it with `Database.resolve` and sets `read`; it has no output. Its App Graph action is on each bookmark's toolbar, through `createTypeExtension`. The article edits the title, the address and the note, and says whether the bookmark has been read. The skill tells the assistant to mark a bookmark as read when the user says they have read it. Bookmarks are created only through the + menu. The inspector passes a reference to the sample for a reference input, shows the sample after an operation with no output, and its sample picker follows the sample's label as it is edited. Supersedes the Save link parts of [D-208].
  date: 2026-11-12
  by: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-208
  affects: [plex-the-plex-plugin, app-framework-define-type, app-framework-add-operation, app-framework-extend-app-graph, app-framework-add-surface, plex-run-in-composer, app-framework-operations, plex-guide-testing, app-framework-publishing]
  why: Save link did what the + menu's create-object already does. Marking a bookmark as read changes an object that exists, which the path did not show, and gives the assistant a reason to run the operation.
```

```mdl
decision D-211: On `/echo` the four guarantee cards sit in two rows of two, and stack to one column on a narrow screen.
  date: 2026-11-12
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [landing]
  why: Three cards and one left a row mostly empty.
```

```mdl
decision D-212: The editor demo loads the Mermaid plugin, and its document has a `mermaid` block that renders as a diagram. Its PLEX narrative says the Mermaid plugin extends the editor through the Markdown plugin's extension capability, and that a plugin can add custom widgets the same way. The canvas demo is titled Infinite canvas, after the plugin, not Architecture diagram, after its content. Its PLEX narrative says other plugins add element kinds and library items to the canvas through its `NodeType` and `LibraryItem` capabilities, and links to Build with a coding agent, which is to get a prompt for building a canvas tool.
  date: 2026-11-12
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-7.5, F-7.10, app-framework-welcome]
  why: The PLEX Overview should show that the plugins are extensible, and name each demo for the plugin it shows.
```

```mdl
decision D-213: The PLEX Overview's What you can build has no list of plugin pieces. After the demos it says they are examples, and that a plugin can add anything a built-in one can, since Composer's own UI is plugins.
  date: 2026-11-12
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [app-framework-welcome]
  why: The live demos show what a plugin can add better than a list, and a list reads as the limits of what is possible.
```

```mdl
decision D-214: Bookmarks' section sits in each space's Content group in the navigation tree, matched with `AppNodeMatcher.whenNavTreeGroup(GraphPath.GroupTypes.content)`. The type, the section and the plugin use the indigo hue. Mark as read has the `toolbar` and `list-item` dispositions, so it is on the bookmark's toolbar and in its menu in the tree.
  date: 2026-11-12
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [app-framework-extend-app-graph, app-framework-define-type, app-framework-publishing]
  why: In Composer the section showed above the groups instead of under Content, and Mark as read was missing from the tree's menu, since the tree shows only `list-item` actions.
```

```mdl
decision D-215: Bookmarks' section is built with `TypeSection.createTypeSectionExtension`, placed in the Content group with `match` and `groupSegment`, and given the URL key `bookmark`. It takes its label and hue from the type's annotations and lists the space's bookmarks, so Extend the App Graph drops its hand-written section and items steps. Amends [D-207] and [D-214].
  date: 2026-11-12
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [app-framework-extend-app-graph, app-framework-guide-app-graph]
  why: In Composer a bookmark in the hand-written section did not open when clicked, because nothing gave its node an address. The type section helper registers one, and it is how Composer's own plugins add a type's section.
```

```mdl
decision D-216: The learning path's plugin is Stash, a reading list like Pocket, and its type is Stashed link. The code names are `StashedLink`, `StashedLinkOperation`, `StashedLinkArticle`, `StashNamespace` and `StashSkill`; the keys are `com.example.plugin.stash`, `com.example.type.stashedLink`, `com.example.operation.stashedLink.markRead` and `com.example.skill.stash`; the section's URL key is `stash`, and the icon is `ph--tray-arrow-down--regular`. Mark as read's input is `{ link }`. Prose calls the objects links. Earlier decisions keep the Bookmarks name they were made under.
  date: 2026-11-12
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [plex-the-plex-plugin, app-framework-create-plugin, app-framework-define-type, app-framework-add-operation, app-framework-extend-app-graph, app-framework-add-surface, plex-run-in-composer, app-framework-publishing, app-framework-anatomy, app-framework-welcome, plex-capabilities, app-framework-operations, app-framework-surfaces, app-framework-guide-app-capabilities, app-framework-guide-app-graph, plex-guide-effect, plex-guide-testing, plex-guide-settings-and-state, plex-guide-using-echo, plex-guide-plugin-manager]
  why: Composer already has a plugin called Bookmarks, and the tutorial plugin should not share its name.
```

```mdl
decision D-217: Each learning path's app lives in a folder named for its section: `src/echo-tutorial` for ECHO's contact book, `src/halo-tutorial` for HALO's, and `src/plex-tutorial` for the Stash plugin. Snippets name them the same way, as `echo-tutorial/...` and `plex-tutorial/...`.
  date: 2026-11-12
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [installation, defining-types, mutating-objects, querying, sharing, guide-react, app-framework-create-plugin, app-framework-define-type, app-framework-add-operation, app-framework-extend-app-graph, app-framework-add-surface, plex-run-in-composer]
  why: The ECHO app's folder was plain `tutorial` and the plugin's was `app-framework-tutorial`, after a section that is now PLEX; naming both by section matches `halo-tutorial`.
```

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

```mdl
ext template
  uri: org.dxos.docs.template@1.0
  desc: A page format, as the ordered parts every page of that template has.
  fields:
    purpose: Prose
    parts: ProseList
```

```mdl
ext page
  uri: org.dxos.docs.page@1.0
  desc: One page of the docs. The inline prose is its summary; the block's position sets its sidebar order.
  inline-prose: true
  fields:
    section: Prose
    route: URI
    group: Prose
    template: ExtRef
    status: planned | spike | done | later
    covers?: ProseList
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext decision
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0
  desc: |
    One decision about the spec, attributed to exactly one actor. The inline prose is the decision
    itself, stated as what is now true, not as the edit that was made.
  fields:
    date: Date                  # YYYY-MM-DD, the day the decision was made
    by: ActorRef                # user:<handle> | agent:<name> — the decider
    for?: UserRef               # agent entries only: the person the agent acted for
    affects?: RefList           # block ids the decision constrains, e.g. [Scene, F-2.1]
    supersedes?: Identifier     # an earlier decision this one replaces
    why?: Prose                 # the reason; on a user entry, only a reason the person gave
    rejected?: ProseList        # alternatives considered and why they lost
    source?: URI                # PR, review comment, issue, or session where it was made
  inline-prose: true
```
